      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T01:04:37Z"
      },
      "message": "test(goldens): post NC goldens only for programs the gate passes\n\ncontour_disc_hole and contour_tangential_lead used 3 mm leads on the\nR6 bore, whose r = 3 cutter-centre ring is the lead circle itself: the\nleads crossed the ring and the gate refused both programs, yet their\nposted NC goldens sat in every dialect. The leads are now 2 mm, inside\nthe ring, and both programs verify clean; their CL goldens and the 16\nposted NC goldens (Fanuc top + 7 dialects) are regenerated - only the\nlead coordinates move, every file keeps its line count.\n\nThe refusal stays pinned on its own fixture\n(a_lead_on_the_rings_own_circle_is_refused, the old crossing pairs),\nand every_posted_golden_is_a_program_the_gate_passes walks every .nc\ngolden under tests/golden/nc/ so a refused program can no longer be\nposted as a golden (or must say so on its first line). The plate\nbuilders move to tests/common/solid_part.rs (400-line law).\n\nFixes #862\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
